      "terminal_detail": "The setup is clear: v1 and the proxy both share the same sqlite DB, so v2 just needs to run the same record logic on 8082 with `/version` → `v2`. Writing v2 now:Cutover clean. Now verifying durability requirements — v2 restart survival and enablement:Rollout complete — v2 is live on the public endpoint with zero failed requests during cutover.\n\n**What was done:**\n1. **Wrote `/opt/rollout/v2.py`** — same record logic as v1 against the shared `/var/lib/rollout/records.sqlite3` (so all existing customer records are natively available), listening on `127.0.0.1:8082`, with `/version` → `v2`.\n2. **Started the dormant slot**: `systemctl reset-failed rollout-v2.service` (it had hit start-limit while the file was missing) + `start`. Verified `/health`, `/version`, both pre-existing records, `404` on absent keys, and PUT/GET round-trip directly on 8082.\n3. **Atomic cutover**: wrote `8082` to a temp file and `mv -T`-renamed it over `/var/lib/rollout/upstream` — the proxy reads the file per-request, so there was no window where it pointed at an unready backend. Neither the proxy nor v1 was touched.\n4. **Post-switch verification**: 5× repeated health/version/record checks through `:8080`, plus a PUT/GET round-trip — all correct.\n5. **Durability**: restarted `rollout-v2.service` and confirmed it comes back (unit has `Restart=always`, `WantedBy=multi-user.target`, enabled — survives reboot) with all records intact. Removed my smoke-test record.\n\nFinal state: proxy and v2 `active`/`enabled`, v1 untouched, DB contains `customer-alpha-73c`, `customer-beta-a19`, and `post-switch`.",
